From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Lech Piekarski <isilweo@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 25 Nov 2026 13:02:58 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: qcom: apq8053-lenovo-cd-18781y: keep the SDHC2
 I/O supply on

The stock DT keeps the SDHC2 I/O supply always on
(qcom,vdd-io-always-on). Mainline has no such option for sdhci-msm, so
mark L12 regulator-always-on.

When the WLAN card is powered off while idle, sdhci-msm can switch
vqmmc off with the card. Resuming the card failed with -EBUSY in about
half of the boots on two units. With L12 fixed at 1.8 V and always on,
one of those units brought the card up on all 30 warm reboots. Fixed
voltage without always-on was not tested.

Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5-5
Assisted-by: Codex:gpt-6.2-astra
Source: https://github.com/isilweo/linux/commit/09788328e59a8d3d90602598f9a36bc13455faed
Base-commit: 1c1a919fd728c881e7ccaf3cf18a3cf3055e0429
---
 arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/apq8053-lenovo-cd-18781y.dts | 1 +
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/apq8053-lenovo-cd-18781y.dts b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/apq8053-lenovo-cd-18781y.dts
index c9ce485920d3..1905b780bd6a 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/apq8053-lenovo-cd-18781y.dts
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/apq8053-lenovo-cd-18781y.dts
@@ -509,6 +509,7 @@ pm8953_l11: l11 {
 		pm8953_l12: l12 {
 			regulator-min-microvolt = <1800000>;
 			regulator-max-microvolt = <1800000>;
+			regulator-always-on;
 		};
 
 		pm8953_l13: l13 {
